 "note": [
  "Scripture source: the Open Luganda Contemporary Bible (OLCB 2017, Biblica, CC BY-SA), parsed from the ebible mirror's USX (bibles/lug_bib), all 66 books. Every quotation was looked up in that verse file and its words copied as they stand (including OLCB's own spellings).",
  "Derived by measurement: a row is mined only when the block contains a 30-character run of that verse (cited references) or a 40-character run (uncited quotations, which Finney mostly leaves unreferenced), compared with quotation marks and punctuation stripped; four coincidental shared phrases were dropped by eye. Rows the translator rendered in their own words because OLCB's sense or wording departs from the KJV the argument turns on (e.g. Prov 14:14, Job 21:30, Acts 9:6), or where the English italics split the verse, are self_rendered. 192 of 211 rows mined.",
  "Conventions: Lecture headings mirror the source caps (h2 'OMUSOMO N.', h3 the uppercase chapter title); 'Text.—' is 'Ekyawandiikibwa.—'; REMARKS is 'EBIGAMBO EBY’OKUFUNDIKIRA.'; citations use OLCB book names in C:V form. Curly quotes as the English; in-word apostrophe ’ as OLCB; site terms Bayibuli, Setaani, Omukristaayo; 'Mr. X' is Omwami X.",
  "Glossary held across the 24 chapters: revival = okuzuukuka (kw’eddiini); measures / new measures = enkola / enkola empya; means = engeri ezaateekebwawo; anxious seat = entebe y’abeeraliikirivu; protracted meeting = olukuŋŋaana oluwanvu; Old/New School = Essomero Ekkadde / Eriggya; temperance = okwefuga mu mwenge. 'Conviction' appears both as okulumirizibwa (early lectures) and okusalirwa omusango mu mutima (later) — a reviewer may want to settle one.",
  "The English source's own slips (doubled or skipped list numbers, commas for full stops, a stray capital) were not reproduced where they would garble the Luganda; numbering mirrors the source exactly so cross-references hold. They are listed in the PR body."
 ],
